§ `Chapters 17 to 19 -- common pleas and assizes`

§§ `Chapter 17 -- common pleas`

-- src:41 | Common pleas shall not follow our court, but shall be held in some fixed place.
@ref Chapter 17 (src:41)
GIVEN `the plea is a common plea` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is held in some fixed place` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A Bar
DECIDE `ch 17 -- the common plea may be held where the King's court happens to be` IS
    IF `the plea is a common plea`
    THEN IF `it is held in some fixed place`
         -- NOTHING-kind (silent): "but shall be held in some fixed place" states where common pleas are held; it does not say that holding one there is allowed (F64c).
         THEN `Bar not covered`
         ELSE Barred
    -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the text does not speak to a case outside the facts this rule names.
    ELSE `Bar not covered`

§§ `Chapter 18 -- the three assizes`

-- src:43 | Inquests of novel disseisin, of mort d’ancestor, and of darrein presentment, shall not be held elsewhere than in their own county-courts, and that in manner following,—
@ref Chapter 18 clause 18.1 (src:43)
GIVEN kind IS AN InquestKind
      `it is held in the county court of its own county` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A Bar
DECIDE `ch 18 -- the inquest may be held here` IS
    CONSIDER kind
    -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): the text names the cases above and does not close the list with "only".
    WHEN `some other kind of inquest` THEN `Bar not covered`
    OTHERWISE IF `it is held in the county court of its own county`
              -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "shall not be held elsewhere than in their own county-courts" (the place is closed).
              THEN `Not barred`
              ELSE Barred

-- "We, or, if we should be out of the realm, our chief justiciar": the sender is the King, or the
-- chief justiciar while the King is out of the realm.  "four times a year" is read as no fewer
-- than four times (fork F18); the text gives no day on which any visit falls.
-- src:43 | We, or, if we should be out of the realm, our chief justiciar, will send two justiciars through every county four times a year, who shall, along with four knights of the county chosen by the county, hold the said assizes in the county court, on the day and in the place of meeting of that court.
@ref Chapter 18 clause 18.2 (src:43)
GIVEN `the King is out of the realm` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party Act
DECIDE `ch 18 -- two justiciars will be sent through every county four times a year` IS
    IF `the King is out of the realm`
    THEN PARTY `the King's chief justiciar`
         MUST `send two justiciars through every county four times a year`
         HENCE FULFILLED
         LEST BREACH BY `the King's chief justiciar` BECAUSE "ch 18: two justiciars were not sent through every county four times a year"
    ELSE PARTY `the King`
         MUST `send two justiciars through every county four times a year`
         HENCE FULFILLED
         LEST BREACH BY `the King` BECAUSE "ch 18: two justiciars were not sent through every county four times a year"

-- src:43 | We, or, if we should be out of the realm, our chief justiciar, will send two justiciars through every county four times a year, who shall, along with four knights of the county chosen by the county, hold the said assizes in the county court, on the day and in the place of meeting of that court.
@ref Chapter 18 clause 18.2 (src:43)
GIVEN `times the justiciars were sent through the county in the year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `ch 18 -- the justiciars were sent through the county often enough` IF
    `times the justiciars were sent through the county in the year` AT LEAST 4

-- "who shall, along with four knights of the county chosen by the county, hold the said assizes in
-- the county court, on the day and in the place of meeting of that court".
-- src:43 | We, or, if we should be out of the realm, our chief justiciar, will send two justiciars through every county four times a year, who shall, along with four knights of the county chosen by the county, hold the said assizes in the county court, on the day and in the place of meeting of that court.
@ref Chapter 18 clause 18.2 (src:43)
GIVEN `number of justiciars` IS A NUMBER
      `number of knights of the county` IS A NUMBER
      `the knights were chosen by the county` IS A BOOLEAN
      `held in the county court on the day and in the place of its meeting` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `ch 18 -- the assizes are held as the Charter requires` IF
        `number of justiciars` EQUALS 2
    AND `number of knights of the county` EQUALS 4
    AND `the knights were chosen by the county`
    AND `held in the county court on the day and in the place of its meeting`

§§ `Chapter 19 -- when an assize cannot be taken on the day`

-- gloss (not the text's): "as many as may be required for the efficient making of judgments" is a
-- judgment, taken as a plain number the person states.
-- src:45 | And if any of the said assizes cannot be taken on the day of the county court, let there remain of the knights and freeholders who were present at the county court on that day, as many as may be required for the efficient making of judgments, according as the business be more or less.
@ref Chapter 19 (src:45)
GIVEN `number of knights and freeholders who remain` IS A NUMBER
      `number required for the efficient making of judgments` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `ch 19 -- enough of the knights and freeholders present remain` IF
    `number of knights and freeholders who remain` AT LEAST `number required for the efficient making of judgments`

-- src:45 | And if any of the said assizes cannot be taken on the day of the county court, let there remain of the knights and freeholders who were present at the county court on that day, as many as may be required for the efficient making of judgments, according as the business be more or less.
@ref Chapter 19 (src:45)
GIVEN `the assize cannot be taken on the day of the county court` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person was present at the county court on that day as a knight or freeholder` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the number already remaining is less than the number required for the efficient making of judgments` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH AN Obligation
DECIDE `ch 19 -- the knight or freeholder who was present remains` IS
    IF `the assize cannot be taken on the day of the county court`
    THEN IF `the person was present at the county court on that day as a knight or freeholder`
         THEN IF `the number already remaining is less than the number required for the efficient making of judgments`
              THEN Obliged
              -- NOTHING-kind (word not the condition here: if because the "if" clause is met here and the case turns on "as many as may be required", which is not a named word (F64c)).
              ELSE `Obligation not covered`
         -- NOTHING-kind (word not the condition here: if because "if" states when the duty arises; the branch is reached by a person who was not present, and the sentence names only "the knights and freeholders who were present").
         ELSE `Obligation not covered`
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "And if any of the said assizes cannot be taken on the day of the county court".
    ELSE `Not obliged`